{"name":"Cherry Bomb","hex":"#b73d3f","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cherry bomb","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spherical, cherry-sized firecracker that generates a high-power explosion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cherry_bomb"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cherry Bomb (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Bomb is a 2011 American action film starring Julin Jean and adult film star Nick Manning, in his first leading role in a mainstream film."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d8/Cherry_Bomb_film_DVD_cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Bomb_(film)"},{"title":"Cherry Bomb (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Cherry Bomb is the fourth studio album by the American rapper Tyler, the Creator. It was released on April 13, 2015, by Odd Future Records. On April 9, 2015, the album was informally announced on iTunes, along with the release of two tracks. Production was handled entirely by Tyler himself, with additional contributions by Incubus guitarist Mike Einziger. The album features guest appearances from Schoolboy Q, Charlie Wilson, Kali Uchis, Kanye West, Lil Wayne, Pharrell Williams and Austin Feinstein, among others. The album was supported by two singles: \"Deathcamp\" and \"Fucking Young / Perfect\", accompanied by 2 music videos."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/26/Cherry_Bomb_Tyler_the_Creator.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cherry_Bomb_(album)"},{"title":"Cherry bomb","blocks":[{"text":"A cherry bomb is an approximately spherical exploding firework, roughly resembling a cherry in size and shape. Cherry bombs range in size from three-quarters to one and a half inches in diameter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/CherryBombGroup.jpg/330px-CherryBombGroup.jpg?utm_